  "term": "cerebral hemisphere",
  "definition": "A cerebral hemisphere is one of the two halves of the brain involved in movement and in functions such as speech, thought, emotions, reading, writing, and learning. Each hemisphere controls muscle movement on the opposite side of the body.",
